+To select CDLS's ordinary FP64 GETRF entry, initialize the pinned submodule
+from `TheCoreTeam/cdls` (`dev-nvi-getrf`) and build it with the HIP plugin:
+
+```bash
+git submodule update --init third_party/cdls
+cmake -S device -B build-mi300a-roc \
+  -DPASTIX_DEVICE_WITH_HIP=ON \
+  -DPASTIX_DEVICE_HIP_USE_CDLS_GETRF=ON \
+  -DPASTIX_DEVICE_HIP_USE_CK_GETRF=OFF -DCDLS_ROOT= \
+  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$ROCM_PATH;$PWD/.deps/hipmm" \
+  -Drmm_DIR="$PWD/.deps/hipmm/lib64/cmake/rmm" \
+  -Drapids_logger_DIR="$PWD/.deps/hipmm/lib64/cmake/rapids_logger" \
+  -DhipCCL_DIR="$PWD/.deps/hipmm/lib64/cmake/hipccl" \
+  -Dlibhipcxx_DIR="$PWD/.deps/hipmm/lib64/rapids/cmake/libhipcxx" \
+  -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER="$ROCM_PATH/llvm/bin/clang++" \
+  -DCMAKE_HIP_COMPILER="$ROCM_PATH/llvm/bin/clang++" \
+  -DCMAKE_HIP_ARCHITECTURES=gfx942
+cmake --build build-mi300a-roc -j2
+ctest --test-dir build-mi300a-roc --output-on-failure
+```
+
+CDLS fetches pinned Composable Kernel headers unless an existing checkout is
+provided through `CDLS_CK_SOURCE_DIR`. An explicit
+`-DCDLS_ROOT=/path/to/cdls-prefix` instead uses a prebuilt installation.
+The default build option remains rocSOLVER; the CDLS plugin identifies itself
+as `hip-hipmm-cdls-getrf`. Each queue owns a handle created by `cdlsCreate`,
+including the rocBLAS state required by the hybrid path above n=4096. Calls
+temporarily bind both CDLS streams to the PaStiX queue and restore the owned
+streams before handle destruction. Workspace remains caller-owned. CDLS's
+ordinary entry does not expose singular-pivot status, so this route reports
+`info = 0` after successful submission.
+
+The `device_cdls_getrf_contract` test covers the hybrid path with n=4161,
+padded leading dimensions, offset matrix views, workspace reuse, queue ordering
+and synchronous/asynchronous calls. End-to-end validation uses:
+
+```bash
+python3 benchmarks/run_ck_getrf_smoke.py \
+  build-mi300a-core/example/simple_solve_and_refine \
+  build-mi300a-roc/libpastix_device_hip.so results/cdls-smoke \
+  --backend-name hip-hipmm-cdls-getrf
+```
 
 The HIP plugin implements the same v3.4 contract with HIP queues/events,
 hipMM async source/pool resources, rocBLAS FP64 operations and either rocSOLVER
